# searching: a `d` that takes longer than 250 ms says `searching…` on the status line, at 80x24
# beside the file name and position, and its answer opens when it comes; merl keeps taking
# keys meanwhile, and a key that moves the cursor drops the search (#1553). app/slow.py is a
# link the walk lists; before each `d` it starts leading to a pipe held open for 5 s, so the
# search by name waits on reading it, as it waits on a big tree, on a machine of any speed.
# One search per pipe: of two readers that wait on one pipe macOS wakes only one at times.
# The last release stands still for those 5 s and never says `searching…`.
size 80x24
merl app/api.py
wait def order_json(order) -> str:
run ln -s ../../slow app/slow.py
wait A slow.py
key t /
type find_by
key Enter
run mkfifo ../slow
run (exec 3<>../slow; sleep 5; rm ../slow; : >../slow; exec 3>&-) >/dev/null 2>&1 &
key d
wait searching…
wait find_by_customer: by name, 3 declarations (3/3)
key Escape
run rm ../slow && mkfifo ../slow
run (exec 3<>../slow; sleep 5; rm ../slow; : >../slow; exec 3>&-) >/dev/null 2>&1 &
key d
wait [code]  searching…
key Down
wait app/api.py  24:19
